<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Velleius Paterculus</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 19 BCE – after 30 CE</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Velleius Paterculus was a Roman soldier and historian who served under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tiberius">Tiberius</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pannonia">Pannonia</a>. His short Roman history in two books, dedicated to the consul Marcus Vinicius in 30 CE, is a contemporary source for the reign of Augustus and the early years of Tiberius, whom it praises warmly. It includes a description of the kingdom and army of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maroboduus">Maroboduus</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/velleius-paterculus.jpg" alt="Velleius Paterculus" width="320" height="480" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Medpro · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:F16-0039-2_(32528546593).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
